# What a CLI deploy must never upload.
#
# `npm run deploy` is `vercel --prod`, which uploads the working directory —
# tracked or not. Without this file that included the 83 untracked files under
# app/, among them a live GCP service-account private key
# (firebase-adminsdk-fbsvc-intrep@intrepid-stage-495117-q1) and app/shared/.env.local.
# Git-driven deploys were never affected; only a deploy run from a laptop.
#
# Keep this list ahead of the app/ tree being tidied, not behind it: the guard
# should hold even if someone re-creates one of these directories later.
app/
archive/
.vercel/
_shared/reports/
# Devices/ holds per-device installer bundles, which are not part of the dashboard.
# The one exception is Devices/sandbox/: it is the Root Directory of the separate
# `channel-sandbox` Vercel project, and Vercel applies THIS repo-root file to that
# project's Git builds too. Three rules each stripped its files before the build
# ran: this `Devices/` (bare, as it used to be), and the unanchored `Sandbox/` and
# `dashboard/` further down. Every channel-sandbox deploy came up empty and served
# NOT_FOUND. It has to be `Devices/*` plus a re-include: git-style ignore cannot
# re-include a child of a directory that is itself excluded. jayti-dashboard
# never builds or serves these files (its vercel.json builds only Backend/ and
# Frontend/), so the re-include only makes its upload bigger. .env*
# and intrepid-stage-*.json below are still excluded inside Devices/sandbox/.
Devices/*
!Devices/sandbox/
Server/
Database/backups/
*.log

# Local env files, wherever they turn up.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Key material, for the same reason as the .env rules above: a CLI deploy
# uploads the WORKING DIRECTORY, not the committed tree, so a private key that
# git never saw can still be shipped. Devices/sandbox/signer.py writes a
# generated P-256 key to disk on first use of the broker path, and
# Devices/sandbox/.gitignore carries the matching rules. Nothing the deployed
# app needs is a .pem — the S24 ingest route reads PUBLIC keys from the
# S24_SYNC_PUBLIC_KEYS env var, never from a file.
*.pem
*.key
keys/
*.broker-state.json

# Heavy local-only trees. A CLI deploy from the laptop must never upload these;
# Git-driven deploys already skip them via .gitignore, but .vercelignore
# overrides .gitignore for `vercel --prod`, so without this the upload tries to
# push ~28 GB (runs/ alone is 26 GB) and hangs indefinitely.
runs/
.venv/
venv/
vscode-office/
node_modules/
.deepsec/
scratch/
personal_folder_agent/
permanent_agent/
jpbir/
.firebase/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.qwen/
.kiro/
.agents/
.claude/
.vscode/
skills-lock.json

# .gitignore already covers these, but .vercelignore overrides it for `vercel --prod`, so a
# laptop deploy would upload them. Database/wa-*.json is the built WhatsApp inventory —
# real contact names from the recovery dump — and nothing deployed reads it. No tracked
# file matches any of the three, so Git-driven builds of either project are unaffected.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
Database/wa-*.json

# Untracked workspace-only files and directories at the repository root.
# In particular, never send service-account JSON or one-off Firestore tools.
.firebaserc
# Anchored: Vercel matches this file CASE-INSENSITIVELY (node-ignore defaults to
# ignorecase), so an unanchored `Sandbox/` also stripped Devices/sandbox/, which
# is channel-sandbox's whole Root Directory. Git on Linux is case-sensitive and
# never showed it.
/Sandbox/
chrome_extraction/
# Anchored: an unanchored `dashboard/` also matched Devices/sandbox/dashboard/,
# which is channel-sandbox's UI (its vercel.json builds dashboard/index.html).
/dashboard/
dataconnect/
eka-runner-private/
eka-runner/
jayti/
_tmp_*
intrepid-stage-*.json
firestore-queue-cleanup-*.json
hash_output.txt
STATUS_SUMMARY.txt
stale_db_inventory.md
stale_db_refs.txt
# Stray agent-prompt file accidentally written to a literal Windows path in the
# repo root. It is untracked and describes live production infrastructure, and
# `vercel --prod` uploads the working directory rather than the committed tree.
# Matched with wildcards rather than spelled out: gitignore treats `\` as an
# escape character, so the real backslashes would need doubling and the pattern
# would silently stop matching the moment anyone re-saved it differently.
*Act as an autonomous DevSecOps agen.txt*
*_REPORT.md
*_SUMMARY.md
*_COMPLETE.md
*_GUIDE.md
*_PLAN.md
*_PROGRESS.md
WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY_MAP.md
REMAINING_REFS_ANALYSIS.md
SAFE_TO_DELETE_FILES.md
yarn.lock

# Isolated device clone test-lab — local-only, must never reach a deploy.
clone-lab/
